# Deliberately NARROW. This repo does not blanket-ignore build output, because some JLib repos
# intentionally commit their x64/ folders so a clone can build without a separate deploy step.
# Only the bench's local artifacts are ignored here: bench.exe is a few hundred KB of binary that
# would bloat history for no benefit, and it is rebuilt by bench/build_bench.bat in seconds.
bench/*.exe
bench/*.obj
bench/*.pdb
bench/*.ilk

# CMake, added 2026-08-07 with the Linux port. Unlike the x64/ folders above these are never worth
# committing: the generated tree is machine- and generator-specific, so a clone that inherited one
# would fail to configure rather than save anyone a step.
build/
# -DJLIBSCHED_STEAL_STATS=ON / -DJLIBSCHED_LATENCY_STATS=ON get their own trees so the normal
# build stays clean
build-stats/
build-latency/
build-latency-stats/
build-compare/
# -DJLIBSCHED_TUNABLE_FAST_SPIN=ON (the lock bench) -- same reason: it is a diagnostic
# configuration and must not be mistaken for, or overwrite, the normal build tree.
build-lockbench/
cmake-build*/
out/
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
CMakeUserPresets.json
cmake_install.cmake

# Measurement harnesses and one-off experiments. Real source, and worth keeping ON DISK -- several
# of these are the only record of how a number was arrived at (scratchpad/taskcost.cpp is where the
# 17.8 ns speculative-split figure comes from, scratchpad/lazytest.cpp holds the negative control
# for the lazy splitter). They are ignored rather than committed because they are machine- and
# question-specific: each one was written to settle one argument, they reference absolute paths and
# a locally-built lib, and a public repo should not carry a graveyard of them.
#
# If a harness turns into something worth re-running on every change, it belongs in tests/ or
# bench/ with a CMake target, not here.
scratchpad/

# MSBuild scratch. $(SolutionDir) resolves differently depending on whether this repo is built
# standalone or as part of the JLib umbrella, so intermediates can land in either place.
.vs/
x64/
Scheduler/x64/
*.user
